              {
                t: 'He agrees with Rabbi Meir on every case.',
                why: 'Then the Gemara’s challenge would vanish — the whole question is that Rabbi Yosei rejects hidden contact.',
              },
            ],
            forged: {
              who: 'Rabbi Yosei',
              text: '“What treading did these pieces touch?” — only a zav’s direct touch would remain.',
              he: 'וְכִי בְּאֵיזֶה מִדְרָס נָגַע זֶה? אֶלָּא שֶׁאִם נָגַע בּוֹ זָב',
              ref: 'Chullin 72b:11',
              url: 'Chullin.72b.11',
            },
          },
          {
            prompt: 'So our mishna knows only Rabbi Meir? Ulla forges the rescue —',
            choices: [
              {
                t: 'Rabbi Yosei argues only over a garment split into its own pieces. But small swatches cut from a large garment — all agree that at the moment of separation they take impurity from their parent. So the flesh takes impurity from the limb at the instant of severing.',
                ok: true,
              },
              {
                t: 'Ulla: indeed, the mishna is Rabbi Meir alone, and the halakha follows Rabbi Yosei.',
